  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HA, Handicapable !</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Handi-capable ! disability is not an obstacle to becoming a full-fledged social actor. The disabled person is an autonomous person able to claim his or her rights and defend them. The project of the NGO Handicaps Avan&#xe7;ons aims to contribute to this idealwhere each person living with disability has access to basic social services to the same extent as others, and is able to express himself andbe listened to by his peers and decision makers. This will be achieved through an awareness-raising caravan on the rights and opinions of people with disabilities, which will include an artistic approach (forum theatre, production of an animated film), and fairground hearings to make it easier for people living with disabilities who do not have civil status documents to obtain them, so that they can enjoy their rights and fully express their citizenship.
At the end of this project Handicaps Avan&#xe7;ons also hopes that the population will be sufficiently informed about the rights and needs of their brothers and sistersliving with disabilities to foster better social relationships and more inclusive and meaningful partnerships.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org ref="XM-DAC-7" role="1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs NL</narrative>
  </participating-org>
  <participating-org role="4" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Handicaps Advance was created in 2021 by people with disabilities who wanted to participate in the fight for change that concerns them. The decision to create the organisation was inspired by the &quot;A toi la parole&quot; project run by the NGO GONI. The membersof the organisation thought that if non-disabled people are committed to their inclusion and to improving their living conditions, then why not themselves? And in 2021 Handicaps Avan&#xe7;ons was born.
The objective of Handicap Avan&#xe7;ons is to contribute to the well-being of people with disabilities at all levels, their inclusion in decision-making components and their efficient empowerment. Handicap Avan&#xe7;ons pursues specific objectives such as - support for the improvement of women&apos;s empowerment (especially disabled women) - support forlocal governance and gender mainstreaming - improvement of the living environment, etc.
The particularity of our organisation is that it is mainly composed of disabled people and works for the benefit of disabled people, their direct and indirect entourage. &quot;Nothing for us without us&quot; is the very reason for the existence of our organisation. It is in the concern of being a direct actor of allthat concerns us that we are committed to create Handicaps Avan&#xe7;ons.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ONG HANDICAPS-AVANCONS</narrative>
  </participating-org>
